From f31da643b1cd0b11657dea664e5dafb2e06c3d2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vita-build <vita@build>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:35:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Vita: program cache takes its programs (uniform locations are
 vitaGL's own), PS1 order in every colour pass, 960x544 by default again

- Program cache: t25's second start took none of the 5 saved programs ("not taken"). Each load
  compared every uniform's location with the saved one, and vitaGL's locations are its own
  values, new at each start. Now a uniform only has to be there (or not) as before; attributes
  must be where they were, and their numbers are bound before glProgramBinary as before
  glLinkProgram (BindAttribs). A rejected one names the check that failed.
- Decals: t25's colour pass gave up the PS1's order past 48 program runs in a batch (solid
  faces, then the rest), which let a floor cover its decal: the flicker left in t25 (graffiti,
  lighting, sometimes). Every batch now keeps the order; the [gl] line counts batches over 48
  runs (each run is a GL draw).
- THPS_R3D_ZNUDGE (t25's trial) is gone: it flickered.
- 960x544 by default again (t25: GPU ~7 ms a frame at 720x408); THPS_VITA_RES=720x408 for the
  lighter one.
---
 platform/pc/README.md           |   3 +-
 platform/pc/include/pc/gl_gpu.h |   8 +--
 platform/pc/src/pc_gpu_gl.cpp   | 102 ++++++++++++++++++--------------
 platform/pc/src/pc_vitagfx.cpp  |   6 +-
 4 files changed, 66 insertions(+), 53 deletions(-)

