 | `THPS_PGXP=0` | OpenGL: both of the above off (`THPS_GL_PRECISE=0 THPS_GL_PERSPECTIVE=0`) |
 | `THPS_R3D_BATCH=0` | OpenGL ES (Vita): a native 3D layer's faces drawn in the PS1's order, split where they overlap (before t20); default: each run of faces between 2D primitives in one depth pass and one colour pass for the opaque faces, then the semi-transparent ones in order |
-| `THPS_VITA_RES=WxH` | Vita: screens drawn at most 512x240, 720x408 (default, t24) or 960x544, scaled up to the screen |
+| `THPS_VITA_RES=WxH` | Vita: screens drawn at most 512x240, 720x408 or 960x544 (default; t24-t25: 720x408), scaled up to the screen |
 | `THPS_R3D_PREPASS=0` | OpenGL ES (Vita), batched 3D: opaque faces in one pass at the true depth (t24; decals can flicker); default (t25): depth first, then colour with the decal tolerance, the no-discard program in both where it can |
-| `THPS_R3D_ZNUDGE=1` | OpenGL ES (Vita), batched 3D, a trial: one pass, each opaque face of a layer moved nearer by up to 1/256 of its depth in the PS1's order |
 | `THPS_GL_DECODE_THREADS=n` | Vita: texture cache pages decoded by n threads on cores 1-3 with the game thread (default 3, 0 = the game thread alone) |
 | `THPS_GL_NODISCARD=0` | OpenGL ES (Vita), batched 3D: no separate no-discard, no-blend program for opaque faces with no transparent texel under them |
 | `THPS_GL_WARMFRAMES=n` | OpenGL ES: frames after a stretch without 3D (loading screens, menus) that decode every texture page they draw, uncapped (default 30, 0 off) |
